#Command 
netstat 

#Description
This command is short for network statistics, used for display several network-related information such as active connections, listening ports, routing tables, interface statistics.
Mainly used by system administrators to monitor network activity and diagnose networking issues. 

#Commands executed 
1) netstat -a : To display active TCP connections along with the external domain names or IP addresses

# Observations
The command enabled me to discover all network connections with my PC, foreign addresses and its state 
such as LISTENING or ESTABLISHED. 








